# Kanban commit-issue cards

When frontmatter `labels` includes **`commit-issue`**, the card was created automatically by `scripts/on_pre_commit_failure.sh` after a failed `git commit`.

Full workflow: [kanban-markdown/SKILL.md](../skills/kanban-markdown/SKILL.md) § Commit-issue cards.

## Who writes what

| Section | Who | When |
| ------- | --- | ---- |
| **`## Problem`** | **Capture script** | On failed commit (hook log excerpt) |
| **`## Failed Tests`** | **Capture script** | On failed commit (pytest test file paths) |
| **`## Staged files`** | **Capture script** | On failed commit |
| **`## Root Cause (current code)`** | **Agent** | When user asks to **review** the card |
| **`## Corrective Action`** | **Agent** | When user asks to **review** the card |
| **`## Label Paths`** | **Agent** | Optional during review (from failed tests / staged paths) |
| **`## Label Methods`** | **Agent** | Optional during review (from traceback, test names, staged paths) |

## Reusable pattern? (on review)

After **Root Cause** and **Corrective Action**, ask whether the failure is a **reusable hook/pytest pattern**. If yes:

1. Add a row to [pre-commit-workflow/reference.md](../skills/pre-commit-workflow/reference.md) § Failure patterns ([agent-self-evaluation/SKILL.md](../skills/agent-self-evaluation/SKILL.md) §6f schema)
2. If a hook-level constraint applies, cite **Signature** in [testing.mdc](testing.mdc) — do not duplicate **Fix pattern** prose
3. Note the promoted **Signature** in **Corrective Action** (or a short bullet below it)

## Workflow gates

| Step | Requirement |
| ---- | ----------- |
| Card created | `status: todo`, `labels: ["commit-issue"]` — user fixes commit or assigns review |
| User: **review** | Agent reads code + card; **prior lessons gate**; fills **Root Cause** and **Corrective Action** — **no implementation yet** |
| User approves plan | User explicitly asks to **implement** |
| `todo` → `in-progress` | Only after user approval; follow **Corrective Action** |
| `in-progress` → `review` | Fix applied; staged `scripts/pre-commit-pytest.sh` green; commit succeeds |

## Card Done — lessons learned

When the user moves a **commit-issue** card to **Done**:

1. Read **Problem**, **Corrective Action**, and promoted **Signature** (if any).
2. Ensure durable patterns live in [pre-commit-workflow/reference.md](../skills/pre-commit-workflow/reference.md) § Failure patterns and [testing.mdc](testing.mdc) when hook-level (e.g. `precommit-ruff-staged-venv`, `agent-no-tmp-venv`).
3. Add **`## Lessons captured (YYYY-MM-DD)`** on `done/{id}.md` listing updated artifacts; run `python3 scripts/build_lessons_index.py`.
4. Area-specific fixes (UI, helpers) → matching skill + rule per [kanban-markdown/SKILL.md](../skills/kanban-markdown/SKILL.md) § Card Done.

## Do not

- Implement on first read — wait for user review approval unless they say **review and implement**
- Use **`## Decisions`** — use **Corrective Action**
- Delete auto-captured **Problem** / **Failed Tests** — append agent sections below them
